---
<main>

<section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
  <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
      <span class="ey">cXML Integration</span><h1>Use cXML to connect procurement and commerce.</h1><p class="lead">PunchOut Central supports cXML for buyer sessions, cart return and procurement transaction workflows.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss this integration →</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#flow">See the flow ↓</a></div>
      <div class="page-proofline"><span><b>✓</b> Free Integration</span><span><b>✓</b> No transaction fees</span><span><b>✓</b> Cancel anytime</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal">
      <div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Integration</span><b>Protocol</b></div>
      <div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>cXML</strong></div>
      <span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span>
      <h3>cXML</h3>
      <p>Procurement connectivity managed through PunchOut Central.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="trust-strip" aria-label="PunchOut Central credibility">
  <div class="wrap trust-strip__inner">
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">★</span><div><strong>Trustpilot 4.7+</strong><span>Customer rating</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">PPAI</span><div><strong>PPAI Member</strong><span>Promotional products industry</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">S</span><div><strong>Shopify Partner</strong><span>Commerce experience</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Connection flow</span><h2>Keep procurement and commerce in their own lanes.</h2></div>
<div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>cXML</strong><span>Buyer / procurement side</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">→</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Authentication, session + transactions</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">→</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier catalog + store order</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sec soft" id="details">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">What PunchOut Central handles</span><h2>The integration layer between the buyer and your store.</h2><p class="lead">Your team keeps the business relationship. PunchOut Central handles the procurement connectivity.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>Buyer connection</h3><p>Configure credentials and buyer-specific connection settings.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>PunchOut session</h3><p>Authenticate the request and open the correct ecommerce session.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>Cart return</h3><p>Send the selected cart back to procurement for approval.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">04</span><h3>Approved PO</h3><p>Receive the PO after the buyer finishes internal approval.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">05</span><h3>Store order</h3><p>Create the matching Shopify order from the approved PO.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">06</span><h3>Visibility</h3><p>Track the transaction and see where an issue occurred.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="proof">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Built for trust</span><h2>Proven enough for the customer you cannot afford to lose.</h2><p class="lead">Simple on the surface. Dependable underneath.</p></div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>90+</strong><span>customers use PunchOut technology built by our team.</span></article>
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>$50M+</strong><span>in order value processed through our technology every year.</span></article>
      <article class="metric metric--dark reveal"><strong>cXML + OCI</strong><span>Buyer sessions, carts, POs, store orders and invoices stay connected and visible.</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Questions suppliers usually ask</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does PunchOut Central support cXML?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>This page reflects the current integration direction of PunchOut Central. Exact buyer-specific requirements still need to be confirmed during setup.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Do we have to replace Shopify?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. Shopify is the current production commerce connector and remains your ecommerce system.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is setup included?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Standard supported integration is positioned as free. Buyer-specific custom development is separate.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-cta">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <span class="ey">A bigger opportunity is waiting</span>
    <h2>When the buyer asks for PunchOut, say yes.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Start with your first enterprise buyer and grow from there.</p>
    <div class="page-hero__actions">
      <a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Connect my first buyer →</a>
      <a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
